1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,350
A useful PrizePicks cheat sheet is not a
list of guaranteed

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:07,810
picks. It is a dated research snapshot
that tells you exactly

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:12,560
who, what stat, which line, what direction
the evidence supports,

4
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:16,490
how strong that signal is, and what still
needs to be

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,820
checked. Start with the identity of the
question.

6
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:23,080
You need the player, team, stat type,

7
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:26,370
and exact number. A lean on more than
eight and a

8
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:29,610
half rebounds is not the same question as
more than nine

9
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:31,880
and a half. If the number changes,

10
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,400
the research may no longer apply.

11
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:39,450
Next comes freshness. A trustworthy sheet
should show when the analysis

12
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:43,220
was produced and whether the underlying
line is still available.

13
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:46,640
A page title that says current is not
enough.

14
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:50,800
The row, its source, and its timestamp all
have to agree.

15
00:00:51,630 --> 00:00:55,483
This capture is a real Propeller example
from August seventeenth,

16
00:00:55,493 --> 00:01:00,020
twenty twenty-six. It shows Christian
Franklin, runs batted in,

17
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,970
a zero point five line, an under
direction,

18
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:05,440
and seventy-nine percent model confidence.

19
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:08,660
Desktop and mobile show the same player,

20
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:11,620
stat, line, direction, and confidence.

21
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:17,390
That confidence score means the available
signals strongly support the displayed

22
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:21,420
direction. It is not a seventy-nine
percent chance of winning,

23
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:23,080
and it is not a guarantee.

24
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:26,140
Now inspect the supporting data.

25
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:30,920
For this dated example, the analysis
included recent hit-rate evidence,

26
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:35,980
park context, usage, market context, and
an injury check.

27
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:40,820
The injury signal specifically said no
injury report data was available.

28
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:43,550
That missing data is part of the answer.

29
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:47,740
A good cheat sheet shows limitations
instead of hiding them.

30
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,280
The evidence also needs context.

31
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:53,360
A recent trend can describe what happened,

32
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:55,380
but it cannot promise what happens next.

33
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,780
Park and matchup information may change
the environment,

34
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,550
but not the final outcome.

35
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:03,960
Market-implied context is not true
probability.

36
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:07,710
And one strong signal should not erase
late lineup news,

37
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:11,200
role changes, weather, or a moved line.

38
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:14,220
Then separate direction from confidence.

39
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:18,200
Direction answers which side the combined
evidence supports.

40
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:22,750
Confidence answers how strongly the model
supports that side for the

41
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:26,140
displayed line. Neither one tells you the
payout,

42
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:31,380
entry correlation, or whether PrizePicks
currently offers that exact projection.

43
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,360
That last point is the required platform
check.

44
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:40,050
Propeller is independent and its public
page is not a PrizePicks-native

45
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:42,340
feed. At the time of this capture,

46
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:47,190
Propeller's current analysis existed, but
the platform-backed PrizePicks line

47
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,760
endpoint returned no matching records.

48
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:53,860
So this row cannot be presented as a
current PrizePicks projection.

49
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:57,160
The correct result is stop, not assume.

50
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:01,420
A cheat sheet cannot establish that the
player is active,

51
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:06,140
the line is unchanged, the projection is
available in your location,

52
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:10,160
the entry terms are favorable, or the
outcome will hit.

53
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:15,490
It also cannot replace the final screen
inside PrizePicks.

54
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:16,620
So use this checklist.

55
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:19,720
Confirm the player. Confirm the stat.

56
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,680
Read the exact line.

57
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:26,420
Check the timestamp. Inspect the
supporting evidence and missing inputs.

58
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:29,160
Read direction and confidence separately.

59
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:34,200
Then verify the actual PrizePicks
projection before making your own
decision.

60
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,940
That is what belongs in a trustworthy
cheat sheet:

61
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:42,550
a clear research question, inspectable
evidence, visible limits,

62
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:44,280
and an honest line check.

63
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:47,740
Propeller is a research and analytics
platform,

64
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:52,020
not a sportsbook, and no model signal
guarantees an outcome.
